Offering him in Gehennom is not a good idea, I'd say; you'd rather
have to return to a co-aligned altar in the upper dungeon, but that's
not worth the delay, and if you're a human and not chaotic that's a
bad idea anyway.

Otherwise it would mainly depend on my character class; as a tourist
I'd tin him and take him with me to the demigod bar, as a barbarian I
might revive or eat him, as a rogue I might throw him into the moat,
as a priest or monk I might bury him, as a wizard I might polymorph
his corpse. But all that has no in-game relevance and would be just
for atmosphere, fun, or roleplaying. ;-)

